 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? It' not rude to ask, and weddings especially can be tough. Do you have a backup plan, like a bubble buddy with you at all times? You could ask for a bubble that includes you and someone else, or just bring along a prefilled epi pen. An epi pen is a little injection you carry for severe allergies. Ask about it at the venue, and always carry it with you. Weddings are supposed to be fun, despite the stress. Bringing small bag of your own food can be reassuring, especially if you' with a group of people you don't know well. You' not being a bother, you' just looking out for yourself. Weddings are supposed to be about the couple, not you. The bride and groom will be thrilled to see you, and the wedding party will appreciate your concern.",
